  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ekta- Advancing Legal Empowerment and Health Equity 
for Marginalized Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ekta &#x2013; Advancing Legal Empowerment and Health Equity for Marginalized Communities is a community-led programme by The Naz Foundation (India) Trust that builds legal literacy and health awareness among LGBTQIA+ people and sex workers, addressing the lack of accessible, accurate, and community-friendly information on identity, welfare entitlements, and inclusive healthcare. The Netherlands-supported component focuses on capacity-building, collaboration, and knowledge exchange between Naz and national and international partners to strengthen the quality and sustainability of community education. Through the co-development of four illustrated, multilingual learning modules on legal rights, documentation, welfare, and protection from violence; a Training-of-Trainers programme for 30 facilitators and 10 master trainers; inclusive facilitation workshops co-hosted with partners such as COC Netherlands; creation of a multilingual Digital Knowledge Hub with verified legal and health information; and peer-learning exchanges linking Naz to international networks, the project combines practical tools with long-term institutional growth. Activities will be promoted via trusted community networks, peer educators, and Naz&#x2019;s social-media channels to ensure safe and inclusive visibility. By 2029, Ekta will have produced four standardized modules, trained 40 facilitators, reached about 3,000 individuals directly and 8,000&#x2013;10,000 indirectly, and launched a digital hub used by community groups and institutions. The project will strengthen Naz&#x2019;s institutional capacity to design and deliver inclusive training, establish sustainable partnerships between Indian and Dutch organizations, and create a replicable model of empowerment. In the long term, Ekta will foster a self-sustaining ecosystem of legal literacy and health equity that enables marginalized individuals to make informed decisions, navigate public systems confidently, and access welfare and healthcare with dignity, turning awareness into action and building lasting inclusion and empowerment across communities.</narrative>
  </description>
